From 559b5aa2bf6245fceb7b4e814ec6b401c2af987b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 22:27:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] mm: convert i_mmap iteration to handle sharded mode

Convert all read-side and write-side iteration over the i_mmap interval
tree to handle sharded mode where the tree is distributed across
multiple shards with independent locks.

In sharded mode, iteration walks each shard sequentially, acquiring
and releasing each shard's rwsem independently. This allows other
operations on different shards to proceed concurrently during the
iteration.

Key patterns:
- Read-side iteration: for each shard, down_read(shard->rwsem),
  vma_interval_tree_foreach(), up_read(shard->rwsem)
- Write-side iteration: acquire all relevant shard write locks,
  then iterate all shards

Modified files:
- mm/rmap.c: __rmap_walk_file with trylock pattern across shards
- mm/memory.c: unmap_mapping_folio, unmap_mapping_pages
- mm/khugepaged.c: retract_page_tables, collapse_file
- kernel/events/uprobes.c: build_map_info
- mm/memory-failure.c: collect_procs_file/fsdax/pfn
- mm/hugetlb.c: huge_pmd_share, unmap_ref_private
- fs/dax.c: dax_writeback_one
- mm/pagewalk.c: walk_page_mapping
- fs/hugetlbfs/inode.c: hugetlb_unmap_file_folio, hugetlb_vmdelete_list
- mm/nommu.c: nommu_shrink_inode_mappings

Centralized mode behavior is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: GLM <glm@linux.dev>
